-- title:
--   Ends, residue discs and valuative cover at q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and an auxiliary guard is fixed: a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`); a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$, where $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`, whose members are exactly the supersingular places $w$ (those that are rational, are affine geometric places, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator $j$ in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$), together with a chosen element $s\in W$; the inclusion `hle` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(X_0(M'))=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of the level-$H$ curve at level $q^2M'$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with surjective residue map onto the reduced field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, cutting out $A$ on constants, compatible with reduction of constants, with the scaling property, and with a place map preserving degrees and pushing forward divisors; and `hR₀`, the coefficientwise compatibility asserting that a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficient image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   On the arithmetic side: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A_0=A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $A_0$ (`hκ`). A second prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. A family $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$, with valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cutting out $A$; an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$; and the cofinality hypothesis `hKcof` that every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in the image of some $K_n$. An element $\pi_t\in A$ with $\pi_t^{q^2-1}=q$, and the tameness hypothesis `htame`: every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with tame character value $1$ at $\pi_t$ fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. Finally a base presentation: $K_b=\bot$ as an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cutting out $A$, and a nonzero generator $\varpi_b$ of its maximal ideal.
--
--   The field $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ satisfying four conditions: (i) $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; (ii) $F_0$ together with the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generates $F$, i.e. $k_0(\overline{\mathbb Q})\sqcup F_0=\top$; (iii) $F_0$ is stable under $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for every index $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` of a primitive $q$-th root of unity and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (iv) a linear disjointness clause: for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a_i$ in $k_0(K')\sqcup F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   For such an $F_0$, and for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, every subring $B$ of $F$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure, the data that the image of the $j$-expansion `jq` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ (`hjR`) and that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ (`hjs`), the membership $\mathtt{jqNModC}(\overline{\mathbb Q},q)\in F$ (the expansion of $j(q\tau)$, `hJK`), an element $a_0\in k_0\cap A$ whose reduction satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q}=s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$ (`hpin`), and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$, the conclusion holds provided the following hypothesis block (one long conjunction; the heaviest clauses are summarised here, none is omitted) is satisfied.
--
--   Clauses on $W_0$: it cuts out $A$ on constants of $k_0$; it is a discrete valuation ring; its maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; the centring clause at $s$: every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, whose order is $\ge 0$ at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $j$ has order $\ge 0$, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose reduction equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue the difference $g-c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; and level-equivariance: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $f,\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f$ both in $F_0$, one lies in $W_0$ if and only if the other does.
--
--   Clauses on $B$ (the affine chart): the $A_b$-algebra structure map is the inclusion of constants; $B$ is contained in $k_0(K_b)\sqcup F_0$ and every element of that compositum is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension $\le 1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi_b$, that is $f\in W_0$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$; the image of $j$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element $b\in B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which cuts out $A$ on constants, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$, and is such that no monic polynomial in $j$ with coefficients in $A\cap k_0$ becomes a non-unit in $V$; and, for each $s'\in W$ with $s'\neq s$, an element of $B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring of $F_0$ that cuts out $A$ on constants and satisfies the centring clause at $s'$.
--
--   The Drinfeld clause: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that the Drinfeld coordinate ring over $\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field $\mathtt{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ inside the Drinfeld function field, with $\#C_s=2\cdot\mathtt{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, kernel the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, agreeing on constants with reduction $A_b\to\kappa$, with every element of the target a quotient of elements of the image, image characterised as the elements coming from the coordinate ring, and equivariance: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ in `hSubgroup q`, $\rho$ of $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}f$ is the `hFunctionFieldAction` of that element applied to $\rho f$.
--
--   The node clauses: $\#\mathtt{nodes}=q+1$; a common chart $B_c$, generated by the $A$-integral constants of $k_0$ together with a finite set, contained in every $O\in\mathtt{nodes}$, with each $O$ the localisation of $B_c$ at the elements of $B_c$ that are units in $O$; the level action permutes `nodes` and acts transitively on it; distinct nodes are separated by an element that is a non-unit of one and a unit of the other; the valuative cover: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that cuts out $A$ on constants and satisfies the centring clause at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates some node $O$ (every element of $O$ lies in $V$, and the non-units of $O$ lie in the maximal ideal of $V$); and, for each $O\in\mathtt{nodes}$, a block of local data (summarised here): $O\subseteq W_0$, $O$ is local and noetherian, cuts out $A$ on constants, and each of its elements is congruent to an $A$-integral constant modulo non-units; there exist $E_0\ge 1$ and a unit $v$ of $A\cap k_0$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{2\cdot\mathtt{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\,v$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit of $O$, an isomorphism of the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A_0$ with parameter the image of $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}\cdot(\text{unit})$, constants go to constants, $c_x\mapsto\gamma_U U$ and $c_y\mapsto\gamma_V V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$, if it lies in $W_0$, is a unit there; the Hasse germ clause, that $j(q\tau)-a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and is carried to $w_V V^{e}$ with $e\ge 1$ for some unit $w_V$; a clause producing a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, cutting out $A$ on constants, a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi_0$, carrying an element whose reduction is transcendental over the residue field (no monic-free polynomial relation with $A$-integral coefficients becomes a non-unit unless all coefficients do), in which $c_x$ is a non-unit and $c_y$ a unit when they lie in $W_x$, and on which the modular functions $g$ as above lie, with membership in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ equivalent to vanishing of the $R_0$-residue and with the centring behaviour at $s$ recorded inside $O$; and a clause producing a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B\cap O$, whose elements have order $\ge 0$ at every place of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ has order $\ge 0$, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at the elements of $B_x$ that are units in $O$, with $F_0$ the field of fractions of $B_x$, with $B_x$ generated by the $A$-integral constants and a finite set, and containing an element lying outside every valuation subring of $F_0$ that cuts out $A$ on constants, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ with the monic-transcendence clause, and fails to contain $O$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every field $F_{ss}$ that is a $\kappa$-algebra and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $F_{ss}$ — a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with surjective residue map to $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, cutting out $A$ on constants, compatible with reduction of constants, and with the scaling property — such that $R$ traces out $W_0$ on $F_0$ (for $f\in F_0$, $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ iff $f\in W_0$), there exists a finite set $N_e$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ with the following four properties.
--
--   First, $\#N_e=q+1$. Second, a place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ fails to lie in $N_e$ if and only if the $R$-residue of every element of $B$ that lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$. Third, every $Q\notin N_e$ carries a residue disc: there are a set $D$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $z\in F$ with $R.\mathrm{IsResidueDisc}\,Q\,D\,z$ — so $z$ is a disc coordinate ($\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of its residue is $1$, each place in $D$ is rational with $z$ integral of residue value of absolute value $<1$, each value in $\mathfrak m_A$ is attained by $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z$ at exactly one $P\in D$, $\mathrm{ord}_P(z-P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z)=1$, and a unit principle holds), the residue map is pointwise compatible on $D$, and the degree formula holds: the divisor of a function with nonzero residue, restricted to $D$, sums to $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of its residue — and in addition every $P\in D$ has $\mathrm{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$ and contains $B$ in its valuation subring. Fourth, the valuative cover of the supersingular tube: for every rational place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that specialises to $s$, in the sense that for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is $\ge 0$ wherever $j$'s is and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose reduction equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$ — either $P$ dominates a node, i.e. some $O\in\mathtt{nodes}$ has all its elements in the valuation subring of $P$ and every non-unit of $O$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ in $\mathfrak m_A$, or $P$ lies in a residue disc off the ends, i.e. there are $Q\notin N_e$ and a residue disc $(D,z)$ for $Q$ at $R$ with $P\in D$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ instance, at a rigid auxiliary level fixed by a prime $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the analysis of the special fibre of the semistable model of the level-$H$ curve along a supersingular place $s$: it produces the $q+1$ ends of the base affine chart as places of the reduced field, a residue disc around every other place, and the dichotomy that a rational place specialising to $s$ either dominates one of the $q+1$ node rings or lies in one of those discs. It feeds the construction of the node presentations, node charts and Hasse germ at level $q^2M'$ for $q=3$.
